  "disposition": "implementation_updated",
  "summary": "Permit capacity specializations to be appended to live C and Metal frame sessions and support explicit execution without trajectory storage.",
  "regressions": [
    "Fourteen C/manifest tests and fifteen native Metal tests pass, including append-after-exhaustion, state relocation, rejected append immutability, finite limits, explicit null limits, trace rejection and u64 step-counter overflow.",
    "Two control-service tests execute compiled C, check capacity failure/read/extend/step behavior and reject modified or omitted hashed artifacts.",
    "A real native multi-collider mesh/joint archive specializes to C with both capacity gates, no trajectory buffers and an explicit null step limit. Its undersized capacity returns required=2/capacity=1 and preserves every uploaded pose bit.",
    "Strict default-feature native all-target clippy and targeted Python lint pass."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "The max_steps field is now an explicit positive u32 or null. Null requires absent Trajectory and FrameIndex storage; missing fields are rejected. Existing finite replay bundles retain their limit. Native frame counters widen to u64 with overflow rejected before mutation.",
    "Appending a trusted specialization validates capacity and persistent-region compatibility before publication. Compilation/allocation still occurs before replacing live state.",
    "runtime_compile.py invokes native upload-only constructors, derives layouts and dispatch, lowers mirrored kernels and records immutable artifact/source/archive hashes. It does not execute reference physics.",
    "runtime_service.py exposes generated-C step, explicit read, extend and close commands; it performs no host physics. Rust public backend selection and automatic growth orchestration are the next integration layer.",
    "No Rust or mirrored TileLang physics arithmetic changed. Full source-bound scene requalification remains necessary; no Ascend device execution is implied."
  ]
}
